    "explicit_deadlock": false,
    "correctness_probe": "ASSUME \\A i,j \\in I : SharedDigitsAux(i,j) = Counted(i,j), comparing the entire functions of row index. Check x=0 with stuttering successor. The checked domains are all 4, 16, 64, and 256 ordered pairs respectively.",
    "recurrence_checks": "ASSUME all ordered (i,j) in I satisfy the function domain RTRows and the source recurrence at every index. Each ring uses B=1 and 2^M IDs. Both operators checked independently, 150 s checker budget, 155 s external cutoff. Every success covers all such pairs; the single stuttering state is only a driver.",
    "four_worker_counted": "Four-node NextMC, counted implementation, A={0}, four workers, CPUs 10-13, 2 GiB checker limit/1900m Java heap, 2400 seconds. Same CFG and properties as the corresponding single-worker run.",
    "prepare": "python3 scripts/perf/scale/lupastry.py lupastryplus.zip DEST --bits M --ready ID... --definition published|bounded|counted --next Next|NextMC"
  },
